From: Shawn Lin <shawn.lin@rock-chips.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:52:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: rockchip: don't ignore clock lookup errors on
 attach
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.2.11
Git-commit: 4c66c423593e26273ea0d644906ed007630c6f6d

commit 4c66c423593e26273ea0d644906ed007630c6f6d upstream.

rockchip_pd_attach_dev() treated every of_clk_get() error as the end
of the clock list, so a clock that exists but is not available yet
(e.g. -EPROBE_DEFER) was silently skipped and the device ended up
without pm_clk management.  Only -ENOENT means there are no more
clocks.

Fixes: 7c696693a4f5 ("soc: rockchip: power-domain: Add power domain driver")
Signed-off-by: Shawn Lin <shawn.lin@rock-chips.com>
Reviewed-by: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Ulf Hansson <ulfh@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
index 490bbb1d1d8e..9706f9950f82 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
@@ -745,7 +745,19 @@ static int rockchip_pd_attach_dev(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd,
 	}
 
 	i = 0;
-	while ((clk = of_clk_get(dev->of_node, i++)) && !IS_ERR(clk)) {
+	while (1) {
+		clk = of_clk_get(dev->of_node, i++);
+		if (IS_ERR(clk)) {
+			error = PTR_ERR(clk);
+			if (error == -ENOENT)
+				break;
+
+			dev_err(dev, "failed to get clock %d: %d\n", i - 1,
+				error);
+			pm_clk_destroy(dev);
+			return error;
+		}
+
 		dev_dbg(dev, "adding clock '%pC' to list of PM clocks\n", clk);
 		error = pm_clk_add_clk(dev, clk);
 		if (error) {
-- 
